19
00:00:47,060 --> 00:00:49,548
Here's the problem that got us interested.

20
00:00:49,548 --> 00:00:52,036
Every year the United States publishes one

21
00:00:52,036 --> 00:00:54,523
average delay, and that single number hides

22
00:00:54,523 --> 00:00:57,011
two different stories. The typical flight

23
00:00:57,011 --> 00:00:59,499
lands about six minutes early, while the

24
00:00:59,499 --> 00:01:01,987
average says seven minutes late, because a

25
00:01:01,987 --> 00:01:04,474
handful of really bad flights drag it up. So

26
00:01:04,474 --> 00:01:06,962
the question is: which story should we

27
00:01:06,962 --> 00:01:09,450
